00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.640 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello everyone so I just came up with  three warm-up exercises for the piano  and I'd like to mention just a few  things about how I came up with them and  why I did so generally speaking they're  all based around parallel intervals or  parallel triads instead of just  transposing them up chromatically I  found ways that I could dovetail each  chord or each interval into the next one  for example for the first one I'm using  both third fingers to shift up so that  it dovetails nicely into the next chord  for the second one instead of just going  up chromatically by major triads I added  a major sixth interval so that again it  dovetails nicely into the next one and I  added that little figure in the left  hand or the right hand depending on how  you're switching it up so that it sounds  a little more interesting for the third  one with the parallel thirds I used to  play it so that all the notes in the  left hand and the right hand are exactly  the same so instead of doing that I  switched it around so it just sounds a  little more crunchy I guess and it just  made it a little more interesting the  hands are closer together it adds a  little bit of confusion so that it makes  it the exercise a little more  interesting to me so one point in  general is that with all of these it  started with a very simple idea I wanted  to work on transposing this tried up and  down or transposing this figure up and  down but I tweaked them all a little bit  so that it's a a little more interesting  to play be a little more fluid from one  position to the next and three it sounds  a little more interesting than what I  had previously or what I could have  the  [Music]  you  [Music]  you  [Music]  with all of these I think I could take  them even further and explore different  patterns different combinations to make  them all the more interesting all the  more fun to play  [Music]  and at the same time being functional as  a warm-up and as an exercise furthermore  I hope you can take little bits of ideas  from this and build your own warm-up  exercises I'll be creating some more  this was very very specific to parallel  intervals but I'll make some more with  arpeggios other chords and other  combinations so again thanks for  watching and I'll see you next time  [Music]  [Music]

